(footprint "PiSocket_2x20_P2.54mm"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "2x20 2.54 mm female socket (JLC C2977589) for a Raspberry Pi mounted UPSIDE DOWN above this board. Two changes from the vendor part. The pads are 1.4 mm rather than 1.6: at 1.6 the gap between neighbours is 0.94 mm, narrower than a track plus its clearance, so nothing can be routed in or out of the pin field; 1.4 still leaves a 0.2 mm annular ring on the 1.0 mm drill, which is JLCPCB's recommended figure. And the odd and even pad numbers are swapped, because a Pi presented upside down shows its solder side and no rotation of a connector can undo a mirror.")
